  "english": "30. Monday. Tone 1 [AK]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Canticle [Harts] of fasting, Tone 8 [DK]: \"O God of our fathers, who art blessed...\" (Astvats harts'n merots bare...).\n31. Tuesday. Tone 2 [BZ]. Canticle [Harts] of fasting, Tone 1 [OD]: \"The children sang in the furnace...\" (Yergein mankunk'n i hnostsin). Say the order of fasting.\n\nIn January:\n4. Saturday. Tone 4 [DZ]. Basil of Caesarea, and his brother, etc.\n5. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ.\n\nSeven-day cycle of the Romans 1.\n\nIn April...\n7. Saturday. Tone 6 [GK]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin Mary.\n\nIn May:\n3. Thursday. Tone 8 [DK]. Day of the Ascension of Christ our God into heaven.\n13. Sunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Feast of the Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Barekendan of the Elijah Fast.\n20. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [A3]: \"Who came for salvation...\" (Vor ekir i p'rkut'yun). See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nIn July:\n1. Sunday. Tone 2 [BZ]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The fasting period [before] is seven days. See in the First Volume until Friday of the third week, which is nineteen days; and come here on Saturday, and celebrate the feasts written below, which are after the Octave of the Nativity.\n21. Saturday. Tone 7 [DZG]. Peter the Patriarch, Bishop Vlas [Blaise], and Deacon Absalom.\n22. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who the heavenly...\" (Vor yerknayin zin). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [DK]: \"When they came...\" (Yorzham yekin), and \"The Angel descended\" (Yev ej hreshtakn).\n\nIn January:\n6. Saturday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ our God. The dispensation of eating [non-fasting period] is nine days.\n13. Saturday. Tone 8 [DK]. 8th Day of the Nativity, and Circumcision of Christ.\n14. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Barekendan of the Fast of Catechumens [Aratsavor]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [DZ]: \"Dawn of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n15. Monday. Tone 1 [AK]. Fast of Catechumens [Aratsavor]. Canticle [Harts] of fasting, see according to the order.\n20. Saturday. Tone 4 [DZ]. Saint John the Forerunner.\n21. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Saint Sargis. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [DZ]: \"Glorifying your holy name...\" (P'aravorelov z'anun k'o surb).\n22. Monday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Sargis and his son Mardiros, and the fourteen soldiers; and the Atomian Generals. Children's Hymn [Mankunk'] Tone 1 [AK]: \"We beseech [You]\" (Aghach'emk').\n\nIn February:\n4. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Great Barekendan [of Great Lent].\n14. Thursday. Tone 1 [AK]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj]. See according to the order in the First Volume up to Vardavar [Transfiguration], keeping the order of this place.\n\nIn March:\n25. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Easter. Day of the Resurrection of Christ our God. See according to the order in the First Volume.",
